      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no convention / I am trying to figure out what the right thing to do is.\n\n* The shared types (e.g. `ColorType` and `DecodingResult`) are not repeated anywhere else, so I am including their doc comments right next to them.  OTOH, the types, functions, and methods from the `extern \"Rust\"` section describe/redeclare Rust types, functions, and methods that are defined outside of the `#[cxx::bridge]` and for those we have a choice whether to provide a doc comment inside the `#[cxx::bridge]` or outside.\n* I think that it is more important to attach a doc comment to real Rust functions, than to `#[cxx::bridge]` declarations.  Rationale:\n    - Doc comments of real Rust functions will be exposed in IDEs (via rust-analyzer)\n    - In theory the doc comments of real Rust functions can be consumed by `cargo doc` to 1) generate HTML docs for the crate and 2) make sure that embedded examples compile and don\u0027t panic.\n\n\nMaybe I should add a short blurb/comment to `#[cxx::bridge]` to say that real comments can be found elsewhere.\n\nDone?  (by adding a short blurb/comment to `#[cxx::bridge]`)",
